A||||12||Patrick's Dad||88 Cradle Dimensions?||||5||
Z||000000||Patrick's Dad||10-31-2001||10:07 PM||||Probably one of the last things I'll do before locking up (figuratively) for the winter is to build a dolly for the engine/tranny/cradle. I'll then be ready to drop it in the spring....<P>I'm thinking putting together a box frame of 2x6's, with 4x4 uprights to contact the "corners" of the cradle. Two stationary wheels to the front (as seen by the car) and two steering wheels to the back will complete the package.<P>Does anyone know the exterior dimensions of the cradle, and how high from the lowest point of the cradle itself are the corners? ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Patrick's Dad||11-01-2001||03:38 PM||||Bump...||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-01-2001||05:56 PM||||I can't answer your question, but I'd be happy to pose one of my own.<P>Do all '88s have the same suspension?  Or just the GTs and Formulas?  Sounds stupid, but I've never owned an '88.  There will be an '88 coupe for sale in the near future.  The motor's worn out (165k miles), the tranny isn't much better, the interior is average and the paint is very dull.  On the other hand, the body panels are in great shape, everything's there, it's got a ton of options (how did that happen?) and the seller will probably sell it for bail money (around $100 if I had to guess).  Might be worth the money just for the suspension (to sell--it's cheaper to modify my '86).||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-01-2001||05:57 PM||||Patrick's Dad--I just realized that I hijacked your thread.  If you want me to delete my post, just LMK.  On the other hand, I've brought the thread back to the top.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
